# VMProtect project policy
#
# This repository intentionally stores no vendor project export because those exports
# bind to a local binary path and can contain vendor-specific protected-function IDs.
# The release environment supplies its project arguments through NWFLASH_VMP_ARGUMENTS.
# Only small Rust build identity, integrity, authorization-response binding, and local
# policy-dispatch functions may be selected. Tauri entry points, WebView, Tokio, event
# bridges, process control, downloads, extraction loops, and third-party code are excluded.
# Do not enable virtual-machine detection or a virtual-machine execution denial policy.
